column5:
The provided documentation does not specify the exact operational loop used to evaluate the Portenta H7 busy-loop current consumption. There is no detailed description of the code or loop structure employed for that particular measurement.

If you need to evaluate busy-loop current consumption on the Portenta H7 yourself, a common approach is to run a simple infinite loop in the main program, such as:

```c
void loop() {
  // Busy loop doing nothing else
  while (1) {
    // empty loop body
  }
}
```

or equivalently:

```c
void loop() {
  // Busy wait loop
}
```

This keeps the CPU active without entering any low-power mode, allowing measurement of the baseline current consumption under continuous CPU load.

However, since the documentation you referenced does not provide the exact loop or code snippet used for the Portenta H7 busy-loop current consumption evaluation, you may need to consult additional Arduino or STMicroelectronics resources or perform your own measurements using a similar busy-wait loop.

Sources:
- Due-datasheet.pdf
- GIGA R1 WiFi-datasheet.pdf
- Mega 2560 Rev3-datasheet.pdf
